[{"year":2009,"total":2764000},{"year":2010,"total":2800000},{"year":2011,"total":2600000},{"year":2012,"total":2100000},{"year":2013,"total":2100000},{"year":2014,"total":3276000},{"year":2015,"total":3290000},{"year":2016,"total":3035000},{"year":2017,"total":2616000},{"year":2018,"total":1962000},{"year":2019,"total":1533000},{"year":2020,"total":1224000},{"year":2021,"total":1187000},{"year":2022,"total":1169000},{"year":2023,"total":1124000},{"year":2024,"total":1031000},{"year":2025,"total":997000}],"footnotes":[{"year":null,"population_type":"STA","text":"Pending a more accurate study into stateless in Iraq, the estimate of stateless persons in Iraq has been adjusted to reflect the reduction of statelessness in line with Law 26 of 2006, which allows stateless persons to apply for nationality in certain circumstances.","view":"asylum"},{"year":null,"population_type":"STA","text":"Pending a more accurate study into statelessness in Iraq, the estimated reduction of stateless persons in Iraq has been adjusted to reflect the reduction of statelessness in line with Law 26 of 2006, which allows stateless persons to apply for nationality in certain circumstances.","view":"asylum"},{"year":null,"population_type":"STA","text":"This figure reflects the number of stateless persons identified through a survey completed by UNHCR and a partner among various communities affected by statelessness, which led to 1,000 interviews being conducted, through which 233 individuals were considered to be stateless. This figure only captures stateless individuals known to UNHCR, while there are likely to be more people in the country who are stateless. It does not include any estimate of the stateless refugee population or persons of undetermined nationality, populations that are also typically included in official UNHCR statelessness statistics. Based on other data sources it is understood that there are also persons of those profiles in Iraq, and the reported figures will be reviewed as more information becomes available.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2015,"population_type":"REF","text":"Includes 33,200 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR in Jordan. The Government estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2015,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR is assisting 18,300 Iraqis at the end of 2015.","view":"origin"},{"year":2015,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 18,300 Iraqis at the end of 2015. The refugee population in Jordan includes 33,200 Iraqis registered with UNHCR. The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2015,"population_type":"REF","text":"Figure at the end of 2015 refers to 33,200 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR. The Government estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2015,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic is a Government estimate. UNHCR is assisting 18,300 Iraqis at the end of 2015. Figure includes 33,200 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR in Jordan. The Government estimates the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2015,"population_type":"REF,STA","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis and Stateless persons in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 18,300 Iraqis at the end of 2015.","view":"origin"},{"year":2016,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR is assisting 16,900 Iraqis at the end of 2016.","view":"origin"},{"year":2016,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 16,900 Iraqis at the end of 2016. The refugee population in Jordan includes 33,100 Iraqis registered with UNHCR. The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2016,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 16,900 Iraqis at the end of 2016.","view":"origin"},{"year":2016,"population_type":"REF","text":"Includes 33,100 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR in Jordan. The Government estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2016,"population_type":"REF","text":"Figure at the end of 2016 refers to 33,100 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR. The Government estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2016,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic is a Government estimate. UNHCR is assisting 16,900 Iraqis at the end of 2015. Figure includes 33,100 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR in Jordan. The Government estimates the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2017,"population_type":"REF","text":"Includes 34,000 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR in Jordan. The Government estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2017,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 16,300 Iraqis at the end of 2017. The refugee population in Jordan includes 34,000 Iraqis registered with UNHCR. The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2017,"population_type":"REF,STA","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 16,300 Iraqis at the end of 2017. Figure for stateless persons is an estimate.","view":"origin"},{"year":2017,"population_type":"STA","text":"Pending a more accurate study into stateless in Iraq, the estimate of stateless persons in Iraq has been adjusted to reflect the reduction of statelessness in line with Law 26 of 2006, which allows stateless  persons to apply for nationality in certain circumstances.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2018,"population_type":"REF","text":"Includes 34,600 Iraqi refugees registered with UNHCR in Jordan. The Government estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2018,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 15,700 Iraqis at the end of 2018. The refugee population in Jordan includes 34,600 Iraqis registered with UNHCR. The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2018,"population_type":"REF","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis  in the Syrian Arab Republic was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered and is assisting 15,700 Iraqis at the end of 2018.","view":"origin"},{"year":2018,"population_type":"REF,STA","text":"Refugee figure for Iraqis was a Government estimate. UNHCR has registered 15,700 Iraqis at the end of 2018. According to some reports many stateless persons were naturalized between 2011-2018, but no official figures are yet confirmed.","view":"origin"},{"year":2018,"population_type":"STA","text":"Pending a more accurate study into stateless in Iraq, the estimated reduction of stateless persons in Iraq has been adjusted to reflect the reduction of statelessness in line with Law 26 of 2006, which allows stateless persons to apply for nationality in certain circumstances. The total reduction of 115 (from 47,630 to 47,515) comes from estimates based on various sources.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2019,"population_type":"STA","text":"Pending a more accurate study into statelessness in Iraq, the estimated reduction of stateless persons in Iraq has been adjusted to reflect the reduction of statelessness in line with Law 26 of 2006, which allows stateless persons to apply for nationality in certain circumstances. The total reduction of 262 (from 47,515 to 47,253) comes from estimates based on various sources.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2021,"population_type":"REF","text":"The refugee population in Jordan includes 34,350 Iraqis registered with UNHCR. The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2023,"population_type":"REF","text":"The refugee population in Jordan includes 28,900 Iraqis registered with UNHCR. The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2024,"population_type":"REF","text":"The refugee population in Jordan includes 25,710 Iraqis registered with UNHCR. The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"},{"year":2025,"population_type":"REF","text":"The refugee population in Jordan includes 8,900 Iraqis registered with UNHCR.The Government of Jordan estimated the number of Iraqis at 400,000 individuals at the end of March 2015. This includes refugees and other categories of Iraqis.","view":"origin"}],"sources":["unhcr_countries","unhcr_population","unhcr_demographics","unhcr_idmc","unhcr_solutions","unhcr_asylum_applications","unhcr_footnotes","wpp_population","natural_earth"]}
